So far terminal::Window is a thin wrapper around a single ncurses WINDOW*:
it lets the rest of the code use ncurses without including curses.h and
adds no semantics of its own. Adding the margin/border functionality of
this objective to it would destroy that thinness. Therefore the
functionality is split over two classes (see the objective description):
the thin wrapper keeps its role under the name terminal::BasicWindow
(decided; other candidates considered: RawWindow, WindowHandle,
NcursesWindow/CursesWindow - rejected for leaking the library name),
freeing the name terminal::Window for the new, margin-aware class of
goal 03, which derives from it (see there).

This goal is the mechanical rename of the thin wrapper to BasicWindow,
with no behavior change at all:

- Rename the class (files Window.h/Window.cxx and class Window, incl.
  Window::Impl, -> BasicWindow.h/BasicWindow.cxx and BasicWindow) and
  update every user: Context (stdscr() and its Window member), Pad (its
  pad_ member; the pad functions newpad/subpad/prefresh/pnoutrefresh/
  pechochar stay on the thin wrapper), the experimental linux0x tests,
  and tests/terminal_paragraph_tests.cpp.
- Build everything and run the full test suite (aap-test) afterwards;
  nothing may change behavior.
